  "result": "All six tests pass (the original four plus the two new ones).\n\n**Changes to `catalog/service.py`:**\n\n- **`find(substring)`** returns copies of records whose title contains the substring, compared with casefold, in creation order.\n- **`export()`** returns a JSON array of records in creation order, built from the existing `list()` output.\n- **`import_(dump)`** parses the dump, validates every record up front, then inserts them keeping their original ids. A malformed dump or an id that already exists in the catalog raises `ValueError` and leaves the catalog untouched. Because ids are sequential integers, the method also advances the internal counter past the highest imported numeric id, so a later `create` can never reuse an imported id. I verified this with a quick script alongside the test run.",
